---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Home">

<div style="background: #f0f9f6; border-left: 4px solid #3abf99; padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #444;">
  🌱 Energy Ledger is just getting started — new content is being added regularly.
</div>

  <section style="text-align: center; padding: 4rem 0 3rem;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 3.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Energy<span style="color: #3abf99;"> Ledger</span></h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #444; max-width: 580px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      Energy systems make claims. A solar farm claims it produced renewable electricity. A company claims it consumed green energy. A prosumer claims they fed surplus heat into the network.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #444; max-width: 580px; margin: 0 auto 2.5rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      But how are they verified? And could they be verified better — with more granularity, more privacy, and more trust — than current systems allow?
    </p>
    <a href="/learn" class="btn-primary">Explore the explainers →</a>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 4rem;">
    <h2 style="text-align: center; font-size: 1.1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: #666; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-weight: 600;">Three questions we explore</h2>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem;">

      <div class="card">
        <span class="pillar-tag">Granularity</span>
        <p style="margin: 1rem 0 0; color: #333;">From annual averages to hourly and real-time matching — how precise can energy claims become?</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="pillar-tag">Privacy</span>
        <p style="margin: 1rem 0 0; color: #333;">Can organisations prove they meet energy targets without revealing sensitive operational data?</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <span class="pillar-tag">Trust</span>
        <p style="margin: 1rem 0 0; color: #333;">What is the difference between administrative trust in an issuing body and cryptographic proof?</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>